		if isPrime(i) {
			fmt.Println(i)
		}
	}
}
```

This program:

1. Reads a single integer `N` from the command line arguments.
2. Iterates from 2 to N (inclusive), checking each number for primality using trial division up to √n.
3. Prints each prime number on its own line.
4. If `N < 2`, the loop body never executes, so nothing is printed (satisfying the "no primes" case).

Example usage:
```
$ go run main.go 10
